From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] Share phone-resident dma-bufs and import phone-decoded
 video

On the socket transport the driver implements VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf and
VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier for the render node's buffers (docs/gpu-buffers.md).
A buffer with CABOOSE_FORMAT_MOD_REMOTE holds no guest pixels: its image is an
ordinary optimally tiled host image, and the dma-buf is only its identity. Its
memory-plane layout is answered from the explicit layout it was created with, or the
nominal one. Within a process, every import or export of one buffer is one host
allocation, sized by the application's request. The first dedicated image bound to a
buffer is registered with the GPU broker so the compositor can present it.

Sync files exported from fences and semaphores signal when the phone has finished the
work: the export submits an empty batch with an internal fence, which a waiter thread
waits through the completion tracker before signalling a vgem fence.

LINEAR NV12 and P010 dma-bufs of phone-decoded video (docs/gpu-media.md) are imported
into device-only memory and filled by latch packets written ahead of each submission.
Their format entries list LINEAR after the remote modifier.

A refused import is reported on stderr as CABOOSE_DMABUF_IMPORT_REJECT with its reason.
